"""Fixed 31-dimensional elemental descriptors for FACTO.

Liu et al. (arXiv:2611.03276) state that scalar features are an affine
map of a fixed 31-component elemental descriptor, but the paper does not
list the components. This table is the Enerzyme stand-in: 17 scaled
properties, a 4-way block indicator, and a 10-way chemical-series
indicator, for Z = 1..94. Row 0 is the dummy element and is all zeros.

Sources are mendeleev (properties, block, series, ground configuration).
Missing Pauling electronegativities and electron affinities are 0.
Missing atomic radii fall back to the covalent radius. Lanthanide and
actinide group numbers that mendeleev leaves empty are filled with 3.
The learned affine layer can reweight any of these channels.
``n_valence/16`` can slightly exceed 1 (the largest valence count in
Z = 1..94 is 17).
"""

